description:
Hello, our name is Customertimes, but you can call us CT. We are a global digital engineering, product development, and technology consulting company. Headquartered in New York, we have a team of 1000\+ experts working across 65\+ countries.










**Role overview:** 




 We are seeking a motivated and detail\-oriented QA Engineer to support a strategic healthcare reporting initiative focused on delivering accurate, reliable, and scalable reporting solutions. The successful candidate will play a key role in validating application functionality, healthcare data integrations, and reporting outputs across technologies including FHIR, SQL, PostgreSQL, SSRS, Power BI, Power Apps, and Azure cloud services. Working closely with cross\-functional teams, the QA Engineer will ensure that solutions meet business requirements, quality standards, and healthcare industry expectations while contributing to the successful delivery of critical reporting capabilities. The role is targeted toward a mid\-level testing professional with experience in healthcare and life sciences environments.










**Location:** 
 Bangalore, India (Hybrid)










**How you'll make an impact:** 



* Develop and execute test plans, test cases, and test scenarios;
* Perform functional, integration, system, regression, and user acceptance testing;
* Validate healthcare data accuracy using SQL and PostgreSQL;
* Test SSRS reports, Power BI dashboards, and reporting solutions;
* Validate FHIR\-based data integrations, APIs, and interoperability workflows;
* Identify, document, and track defects through resolution;
* Verify end\-to\-end business processes and reporting workflows;
* Collaborate with developers, business analysts, and stakeholders to ensure quality delivery;
* Support testing activities for Azure cloud\-based applications and services;
* Maintain test documentation and supporting quality evidence.









**What makes you a great fit:** 



* 3\+ years of experience in Software Quality Assurance and application testing;
* Strong experience with manual testing methodologies;
* Proficiency in SQL and database validation techniques;
* Experience testing reporting platforms such as SSRS and Power BI;
* Familiarity with PostgreSQL and API/integration testing;
* Working knowledge of Azure cloud environments;
* Understanding of healthcare data and healthcare/life sciences business processes;
* Strong analytical, problem\-solving, communication, and collaboration skills;
* Bachelor’s degree in computer science, Engineering, Information Systems, or a related discipline (or equivalent experience).









**Preferred qualifications:** 



* Experience with FHIR standards and healthcare interoperability testing;
* Prior experience supporting FHIR implementations;
* Familiarity with Power Apps testing;
* Exposure to test automation frameworks and automation concepts;
* Experience working within regulated healthcare environments.









**Key skills:** 




 FHIR, SQL, PostgreSQL, SSRS, Power BI, Power Apps, Azure Cloud, Manual Testing, API Testing, Healthcare Data Validation, Defect Management, UAT, Regression Testing, Healthcare \& Life Sciences Domain Knowledge.










**Must have:** 




 Database Testing (Snowflake), FHIR, Power BI Report Validation, Automation, Manual Testing.










**Good to have:** 




 Healthcare \& Life Sciences Domain Knowledge, API Testing, Azure Cloud, AWS, SQL, PostgreSQL, SSRS.










 If you're looking to contribute to global projects, grow your skills, shape the way you work, and be part of a connected international community — Customertimes is the place to build your next career chapter. Are you ready to spark the tech with us?










 Share your updated CV with reshma.ponnamma@customertimes.com
